HAND-WRITTEN, NOT RECORDED.

lsp-languages.json is what `kiln lsp --languages --format json` should
print for a project whose [code] paths hold Rust and Tcl files. It was
written by hand from Kiln's unreleased, unverified commit 4592faf ("Lsp:
kiln lsp --languages says what init --fenix would register", never
compiled): its test `lsp_languages_lists_what_init_fenix_would_register`
expects exactly these keys and values, and kiln's `json_out` prints keys
in name order, two spaces deep, as its other answers in ../out/ are.

No released kiln prints it yet (kiln 1.0.0 refuses --languages; its real
refusal is recorded in ../out/demo/lsp-languages.*). Once a kiln that has
it is released, record.sh records the real answer in ../out/, and the
tests should read that instead of this file.
